(window.LEARNC_DATA = window.LEARNC_DATA || []).push({"day": 7, "title": "Day 7", "sub": "Strings: char, strlen, strcmp, counting characters", "plan": "About 20 minutes of theory, 15 minutes reading and running the 2 examples, and 60 to 90 minutes on the 4 exercises. Exercises 3 and 4 work on strings of up to 10<sup>6</sup> characters, so the code must be efficient.", "goals": ["Understand that a string in C is an array of <code>char</code> ended by <code>'\\0'</code>, and read, print and loop over it.", "Treat characters as small numbers: <code>s[i] - 'a'</code> gives a position from 0 to 25, which is the key to counting letters.", "Use <code>strlen</code> and <code>strcmp</code> correctly, and know why <code>==</code> does not compare strings.", "Read a whole line with spaces using <code>fgets</code>, and apply sliding-window counting to long strings."], "theory": [{"title": "Characters and strings", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>A <code>char</code> is a small integer (one byte) that stands for a character. The character <code>'a'</code> is the number 97, <code>'b'</code> is 98, ..., <code>'z'</code> is 122; <code>'A'</code> is 65 and <code>'0'</code> is 48. Letters and digits are in consecutive order, so <code>'c' - 'a'</code> is 2 and <code>'7' - '0'</code> is 7.</p>\n<p>A <b>string</b> is an array of <code>char</code> whose last meaningful element is followed by the special character <code>'\\0'</code> (the number 0). This marker tells functions where the text ends. So an array for a word of up to 100 letters must have <b>101</b> elements: one extra for the <code>'\\0'</code>. <code>scanf(\"%s\", s)</code> reads one word (it stops at a space or newline), writes it into <code>s</code> and adds the <code>'\\0'</code> itself. There is no <code>&amp;</code> before <code>s</code>, because an array name already stands for the array. <code>strlen(s)</code> (from <code>&lt;string.h&gt;</code>) counts the characters before the <code>'\\0'</code>.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">char</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">101</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// 100 letters + the '\\0'</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">strlen</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"length = %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"s[%d] = '%c', code %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// %c: as a character, %d: as a number</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// make it uppercase</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'a'</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'z'</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'a'</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'A'</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// %s prints the whole string</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char s[101];                 // 100 letters + the '\\0'\n    scanf(\"%s\", s);\n\n    int n = strlen(s);\n    printf(\"length = %d\\n\", n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        printf(\"s[%d] = '%c', code %d\\n\", i, s[i], s[i]);   // %c: as a character, %d: as a number\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {                  // make it uppercase\n        if (s[i] >= 'a' && s[i] <= 'z') {\n            s[i] = s[i] - 'a' + 'A';\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", s);           // %s prints the whole string\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "Cab", "out": "length = 3\ns[0] = 'C', code 67\ns[1] = 'a', code 97\ns[2] = 'b', code 98\nCAB"}, {"in": "hello", "out": "length = 5\ns[0] = 'h', code 104\ns[1] = 'e', code 101\ns[2] = 'l', code 108\ns[3] = 'l', code 108\ns[4] = 'o', code 111\nHELLO"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box warn\"><b>Take care.</b> Evaluate <code>strlen(s)</code> <b>once</b> and keep it in a variable. Writing <code>i &lt; strlen(s)</code> in the loop condition makes C count the whole string again at every step, which is slow for a string of 10<sup>6</sup> characters. Also, an array that is too small is not detected: a longer word silently overwrites the memory after it.</div>"}]}, {"title": "Counting characters", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>This is the frequency array of Day 3, with the characters as indexes. For a lowercase letter <code>c</code>, the expression <code>c - 'a'</code> is a number from 0 to 25 (<code>'a'</code> is 0, <code>'b'</code> is 1, ...). So <code>freq[26]</code> can store how many times each letter appears: add 1 at <code>freq[s[i] - 'a']</code> for every character. One pass over the string, and every question about &ldquo;how many of this letter&rdquo; is answered immediately.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">char</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">1001</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">strlen</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">freq</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">26</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">};</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// freq[0] counts 'a', freq[1] counts 'b', ...</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">freq</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'a'</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">26</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">freq</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%c: %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'a'</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">freq</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-p\">]);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// number c back to a letter</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char s[1001];\n    scanf(\"%s\", s);\n    int n = strlen(s);\n\n    int freq[26] = {0};                  // freq[0] counts 'a', freq[1] counts 'b', ...\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        freq[s[i] - 'a']++;\n    }\n\n    for (int c = 0; c < 26; c++) {\n        if (freq[c] > 0) {\n            printf(\"%c: %d\\n\", 'a' + c, freq[c]);    // number c back to a letter\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "banana", "out": "a: 3\nb: 1\nn: 2"}, {"in": "mississippi", "out": "i: 4\nm: 1\np: 2\ns: 4"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Things to notice.</b> The conversion works in both directions: <code>s[i] - 'a'</code> turns a letter into an index, and <code>'a' + c</code> turns an index back into a letter. This version assumes that the string has only lowercase letters; with other characters the index would leave the array. If the string can contain uppercase letters or digits, make the array bigger (for example <code>freq[256]</code> and use <code>freq[(unsigned char) s[i]]</code>).</div>"}]}, {"title": "Comparing strings", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>Never compare two strings with <code>==</code>: that compares the <i>addresses</i> of the two arrays, not their contents, so it is always false for two different arrays. Use <code>strcmp(a, b)</code> from <code>&lt;string.h&gt;</code>. It returns <b>0</b> when the strings are equal, a <b>negative</b> number when <code>a</code> comes before <code>b</code> in dictionary order, and a <b>positive</b> number when <code>a</code> comes after <code>b</code>. The order is by character code, so every uppercase letter comes before every lowercase letter (<code>'Z'</code> is 90, <code>'a'</code> is 97). Do not test for a specific value such as 1 or -1; test only the sign: <code>&lt; 0</code>, <code>== 0</code>, <code>&gt; 0</code>.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">char</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">101</span><span class=\"p-p\">],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">101</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s %s\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">strcmp</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">==</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"equal</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">else</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s comes first</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">else</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s comes first</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char a[101], b[101];\n    scanf(\"%s %s\", a, b);\n\n    int r = strcmp(a, b);\n    if (r == 0) printf(\"equal\\n\");\n    else if (r < 0) printf(\"%s comes first\\n\", a);\n    else printf(\"%s comes first\\n\", b);\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "apple apple", "out": "equal"}, {"in": "apple banana", "out": "apple comes first"}, {"in": "b a", "out": "a comes first"}, {"in": "app apple", "out": "app comes first"}, {"in": "Zebra apple", "out": "Zebra comes first"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Things to notice.</b> <code>&quot;app&quot;</code> comes before <code>&quot;apple&quot;</code>: when one string is the beginning of the other, the shorter one is smaller. <code>&quot;Zebra&quot;</code> comes before <code>&quot;apple&quot;</code> because of the character codes. To copy a string use <code>strcpy(dest, src)</code>; the statement <code>dest = src</code> does not work for arrays.</div>"}]}, {"title": "Reading a whole line", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p><code>scanf(\"%s\")</code> stops at the first space, so it cannot read a sentence. Use <code>fgets(line, size, stdin)</code>: it reads a full line, up to <code>size - 1</code> characters, and <b>keeps the newline</b> <code>'\\n'</code> at the end of the text if the line fits. Usually you remove it:</p>"}, {"t": "snippet", "html": "<span class=\"p-kt\">char</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">1001</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-n\">fgets</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">stdin</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">strlen</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">==</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'\\n'</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'\\0'</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// cut the newline: the string is now one character shorter</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-o\">--</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "char line[1001];\nfgets(line, sizeof line, stdin);\nint n = strlen(line);\nif (n > 0 && line[n - 1] == '\\n') {\n    line[n - 1] = '\\0';              // cut the newline: the string is now one character shorter\n    n--;\n}"}, {"t": "html", "html": "<p>A common trap: after <code>scanf(\"%d\", &amp;k)</code> the newline that ends that line is still waiting in the input, so a following <code>fgets</code> would read an <i>empty line</i>. Read and throw away the rest of the first line before calling <code>fgets</code>:</p>"}, {"t": "snippet", "html": "<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">k</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">k</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">ch</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-k\">while</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">((</span><span class=\"p-n\">ch</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">getchar</span><span class=\"p-p\">())</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">!=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'\\n'</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">ch</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">!=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">EOF</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// skip the rest of the first line</span>\n<span class=\"p-n\">fgets</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">stdin</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// now it reads the real second line</span>", "raw": "int k;\nscanf(\"%d\", &k);\nint ch;\nwhile ((ch = getchar()) != '\\n' && ch != EOF) { }   // skip the rest of the first line\nfgets(line, sizeof line, stdin);                    // now it reads the real second line"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">char</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">1001</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">fgets</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">stdin</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">strlen</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">==</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'\\n'</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'\\0'</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-o\">--</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">words</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">inWord</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// inWord = 1 while we are inside a word</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">line</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">!=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">' '</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-o\">!</span><span class=\"p-n\">inWord</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">                </span><span class=\"p-n\">words</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// a new word starts here</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">inWord</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">else</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">inWord</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d characters, %d words</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">words</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char line[1001];\n    fgets(line, sizeof line, stdin);\n    int n = strlen(line);\n    if (n > 0 && line[n - 1] == '\\n') {\n        line[n - 1] = '\\0';\n        n--;\n    }\n\n    int words = 0, inWord = 0;           // inWord = 1 while we are inside a word\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (line[i] != ' ') {\n            if (!inWord) words++;        // a new word starts here\n            inWord = 1;\n        } else {\n            inWord = 0;\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d characters, %d words\\n\", n, words);\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "the quick  brown fox", "out": "20 characters, 4 words"}, {"in": "hello", "out": "5 characters, 1 words"}, {"in": "   spaces   around   ", "out": "21 characters, 2 words"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Things to notice.</b> The words are counted at the moment each one <i>starts</i> (a non-space after a space or at the beginning), so several spaces in a row do not create extra words.</div>"}]}], "examples": [{"title": "Palindrome check", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>A word is a <b>palindrome</b> if it reads the same backwards (<code>level</code>, <code>noon</code>). Use two indexes: <code>i</code> from the left end and <code>j</code> from the right end. Compare the two characters, move both toward the middle, and stop at the first difference. This is the two-pointer idea of Day 4, now on a string.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">char</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">100001</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">strlen</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">ok</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">while</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">!=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-p\">])</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">ok</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-k\">break</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-o\">--</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">ok</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">?</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-s\">\"YES\"</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">:</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-s\">\"NO\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char s[100001];\n    scanf(\"%s\", s);\n    int n = strlen(s);\n\n    int i = 0, j = n - 1;\n    int ok = 1;\n    while (i < j) {\n        if (s[i] != s[j]) {\n            ok = 0;\n            break;\n        }\n        i++;\n        j--;\n    }\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", ok ? \"YES\" : \"NO\");\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "level", "out": "YES"}, {"in": "abca", "out": "NO"}, {"in": "a", "out": "YES"}, {"in": "abcba", "out": "YES"}, {"in": "ab", "out": "NO"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Things to notice.</b> Single characters are compared with <code>!=</code>, which is fine: a <code>char</code> is a number. Only whole strings need <code>strcmp</code>. A word of length 1 is always a palindrome because the loop does not run at all. Only half of the word is visited.</div>"}]}, {"title": "Are two words anagrams?", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>Two words are <b>anagrams</b> if one can be obtained from the other by rearranging the letters (<code>listen</code> and <code>silent</code>). Sorting both words would work, but counting is simpler and faster: add 1 to <code>cnt[c]</code> for each letter of the first word and subtract 1 for each letter of the second. If the words are anagrams, every counter ends at exactly 0.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">char</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">1001</span><span class=\"p-p\">],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">1001</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s %s\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">cnt</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">26</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">!=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'\\0'</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">cnt</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'a'</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// a loop can also stop at the '\\0'</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">!=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'\\0'</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">cnt</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">b</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-sc\">'a'</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-o\">--</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">ok</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">26</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">cnt</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">!=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">ok</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%s</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">ok</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">?</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-s\">\"YES\"</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">:</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-s\">\"NO\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char a[1001], b[1001];\n    scanf(\"%s %s\", a, b);\n\n    int cnt[26] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; a[i] != '\\0'; i++) cnt[a[i] - 'a']++;    // a loop can also stop at the '\\0'\n    for (int i = 0; b[i] != '\\0'; i++) cnt[b[i] - 'a']--;\n\n    int ok = 1;\n    for (int c = 0; c < 26; c++) {\n        if (cnt[c] != 0) ok = 0;\n    }\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", ok ? \"YES\" : \"NO\");\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "listen silent", "out": "YES"}, {"in": "abc abd", "out": "NO"}, {"in": "aab aba", "out": "YES"}, {"in": "a aa", "out": "NO"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Things to notice.</b> The loop <code>for (int i = 0; a[i] != '\\0'; i++)</code> walks to the end of the string without calling <code>strlen</code>. Words of different lengths are rejected automatically: the counters cannot all return to 0. This &ldquo;add for one side, subtract for the other&rdquo; trick for comparing the contents of two collections is useful in the last exercise.</div>"}]}], "exercises": [{"title": "Vowels, consonants and the reverse", "level": "Easy", "cls": "easy", "use": "Sections 1, 2", "statement": "Given a word made of lowercase letters, print how many vowels (<code>a e i o u</code>) and how many consonants it has, and then the word written backwards.", "input": ["One line with a word of lowercase English letters (length from 1 to 10<sup>5</sup>)."], "output": ["Line 1: the number of vowels and the number of consonants, separated by a space.", "Line 2: the word reversed."], "extra": "", "examples": [{"in": "programming", "out": "3 8\ngnimmargorp"}, {"in": "aeiou", "out": "5 0\nuoiea"}, {"in": "xyz", "out": "0 3\nzyx"}, {"in": "banana", "out": "3 3\nananab"}]}, {"title": "Caesar cipher", "level": "Easy - Medium", "cls": "easymed", "use": "Sections 1, 4, Day 2 (remainders)", "statement": "A <b>Caesar cipher</b> replaces every letter by the letter k places later in the alphabet, going back to the start after <code>z</code> (so with k = 3: <code>a</code> becomes <code>d</code>, <code>x</code> becomes <code>a</code>). Uppercase letters stay uppercase and lowercase stay lowercase. Every other character (spaces, digits, punctuation) is left unchanged.<br><br>Given k and a line of text, print the encrypted text. k can be negative: then the letters move backwards.", "input": ["Line 1: an integer k (&minus;10<sup>9</sup> &le; k &le; 10<sup>9</sup>).", "Line 2: a line of text with letters, digits, spaces and punctuation. Its length is from 1 to 10<sup>5</sup>, and it does not begin or end with a space."], "output": ["One line: the encrypted text."], "extra": "The text can contain spaces, so <code>scanf(\"%s\")</code> will not read it. Remember the newline that stays in the input after the number.", "examples": [{"in": "3\nHello, World!", "out": "Khoor, Zruog!"}, {"in": "-1\nabc XYZ", "out": "zab WXY"}, {"in": "26\nNothing changes 123.", "out": "Nothing changes 123."}, {"in": "1000000000\nabc", "out": "mno"}, {"in": "-1000000000\nabc", "out": "opq"}]}, {"title": "Run-length encoding", "level": "Medium", "cls": "med", "use": "Sections 1, 2, Day 3 (scanning an array)", "statement": "A <b>run</b> is a maximal block of equal consecutive characters. In <code>aabbbaaaa</code> the runs are <code>aa</code>, <code>bbb</code>, <code>aaaa</code>.<br><br>For a given string, print its <b>run-length encoding</b>: for every run, in order, the letter followed by the length of the run, all written together (<code>aabbbaaaa</code> becomes <code>a2b3a4</code>; a run of length 1 is also written with its length). Then print the <b>longest run</b>: its letter and its length. If several runs have the maximum length, print the one that appears first.<br><br><b>Time limit:</b> about 1 second.", "input": ["One line with a string of lowercase English letters (length from 1 to 10<sup>6</sup>)."], "output": ["Line 1: the encoded string.", "Line 2: the letter and the length of the longest run, separated by a space."], "extra": "The encoded string can be longer than 10<sup>6</sup> characters (each run adds a number): do not build it in an array of the wrong size. You can print it piece by piece as you go.", "examples": [{"in": "aaabcc", "out": "a3b1c2\na 3"}, {"in": "z", "out": "z1\nz 1"}, {"in": "aabbbaaaa", "out": "a2b3a4\na 4"}, {"in": "abab", "out": "a1b1a1b1\na 1"}, {"in": "aabb", "out": "a2b2\na 2"}]}, {"title": "Anagram windows", "level": "Hard", "cls": "hard", "use": "Sections 2, 3, Example 2, Day 3 (prefix sums) and Day 4 (two pointers)", "statement": "You are given a text T and a pattern P. A <b>window</b> is a block of |P| consecutive characters of T (starting at position i, with positions numbered from 0). Count the windows that are an <b>anagram</b> of P (the same letters with the same counts, in any order), and print the position of the first such window, or &minus;1 if there is none.<br><br><b>Time limit:</b> about 1 second. Sorting or counting the letters of every window from scratch takes about |T| &middot; |P| steps, which is far too slow when both strings are long.", "input": ["Line 1: the text T, lowercase English letters, length from 1 to 10<sup>6</sup>.", "Line 2: the pattern P, lowercase English letters, length from 1 to |T|."], "output": ["Two integers separated by a space: the number of windows that are an anagram of P, and the position of the first one (or &minus;1)."], "extra": "", "examples": [{"in": "cbaebabacd\nabc", "out": "2 0"}, {"in": "aaaa\naa", "out": "3 0"}, {"in": "abc\nd", "out": "0 -1"}, {"in": "hello\nhello", "out": "1 0"}, {"in": "abab\nba", "out": "3 0"}, {"in": "xxabcxx\ncab", "out": "1 2"}]}]});
